Subject: [REVIEW 01/09] Qualcomm USB4 PHY modes, tables and lifecycle

Add the Thunderbolt PHY interface and the QMP USB4 mode, Glymur register tables, and PHY power/reset sequencing. Review mode transitions and ownership of shared USB/DP lanes. A Type-C mode requested while USB4 owns the PHY, such as DisplayPort alternate mode, is applied when USB4 releases it.

Dependencies: Base prerequisites. Used by patches 04 and 05.

Source attribution: Konrad Dybcio USB4 PHY v5 plus local Glymur/lifecycle adaptations; original headers in provenance/usb4/00-usb4phy-v5-konrad-dybcio.mbox and deltas 01-07.

This is a review grouping of preserved source, not a new authorship claim or
an independently build-validated upstream commit. Original attribution remains
in the referenced provenance files. No new Signed-off-by trailers are added.

